The step drawer reads the normalized step and its ioContracts with the flow contractDefinitions. It shows a heading per contract, exact field tables and separate JSON examples, including authority and projection/source labels. It shows the authored narrative once and hides generated compatibility text/badges when valid structured metadata is present. Missing metadata or a shape the display guard cannot use keeps the readable fallback; full repository validation remains separate. Live AC references, mock records and screen titles remain available; opening the drawer changes local selection, not repository data. [Drawer](leafcutter-web/components/flows/flow-drawer.tsx).

The inspector groups consumed and produced contract fields with their exact keys, types, requiredness and defaults. It shows raw JSON examples with full/projection and provenance labels, preserves the narrative once, and retains the legacy view when structured metadata is unavailable or unusable.

